  "id": "paroxysmal-sleep",
  "term": "paroxysmal sleep",
  "definition": "Paroxysmal sleep is a condition marked by repeated episodes of excessive daytime sleepiness and brief lapses into sleep or consciousness, sometimes with automatic behavior and later memory gaps. It is often accompanied by cataplexy, sleep paralysis, and vivid experiences as sleep begins.",
